WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.980
Before you begin, make sure you are somewhere you can safely give part of your attention to this practice.

2
00:00:06.680 --> 00:00:09.560
Keep your eyes open if you need to stay oriented.

3
00:00:11.960 --> 00:00:14.700
Pressure can make everything seem equally urgent.

4
00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:19.700
For these minutes, you do not need to solve the whole situation.

5
00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:26.400
Begin by noticing one fact: you are here, in this place, in this body.

6
00:00:47.693 --> 00:00:49.043
Feel the support beneath you.

7
00:00:50.743 --> 00:00:54.613
Let your feet meet the floor, or notice the weight of your body on the chair or bed.

8
00:00:56.313 --> 00:00:59.533
Name three things you can see without searching for anything special.

9
00:01:26.150 --> 00:01:27.360
Now hear two sounds.

10
00:01:29.060 --> 00:01:31.210
One may be near and one farther away.

11
00:01:32.910 --> 00:01:37.820
Let sound remind you that this moment is larger than the demand occupying your mind.

12
00:02:04.436 --> 00:02:06.656
Notice one place in the body that is working hard.

13
00:02:08.356 --> 00:02:12.046
Perhaps the jaw, the shoulders, the hands, or the belly.

14
00:02:13.746 --> 00:02:15.706
You do not have to make it relax.

15
00:02:17.406 --> 00:02:20.586
Ask only whether five percent less effort is available.

16
00:02:52.526 --> 00:02:53.906
Let the breath remain natural.

17
00:02:55.606 --> 00:02:58.046
On an inhale, silently say, here.

18
00:02:59.746 --> 00:03:02.176
On an exhale, silently say, now.

19
00:03:03.876 --> 00:03:08.056
If those words do not help, simply feel one full breath from beginning to end.

20
00:03:55.966 --> 00:03:58.506
Thoughts about what must happen next may return.

21
00:04:00.206 --> 00:04:05.026
You can acknowledge them: planning is here, worry is here, urgency is here.

22
00:04:06.726 --> 00:04:09.566
Then return to the contact of your body with support.

23
00:04:49.490 --> 00:04:52.900
Choose one demand that can wait for the length of three breaths.

24
00:04:54.600 --> 00:04:55.280
Not forever.

25
00:04:56.980 --> 00:04:58.140
Just three breaths.

26
00:05:46.050 --> 00:05:51.400
Now ask a practical question: what is the next workable action, not every action?

27
00:05:53.100 --> 00:05:59.550
It may be sending one message, writing one line, asking for help, drinking water, or taking a longer pause.

28
00:06:01.250 --> 00:06:03.050
You do not need the perfect answer.

29
00:06:34.990 --> 00:06:38.690
Feel both feet or another steady point.

30
00:06:40.390 --> 00:06:41.490
Notice the room again.

31
00:06:43.190 --> 00:06:44.160
Let your gaze move.

32
00:06:45.860 --> 00:06:47.400
Take in one more ordinary breath.

33
00:06:49.800 --> 00:06:51.240
The pressure may still be present.

34
00:06:52.940 --> 00:06:55.180
This pause does not promise to remove it.

35
00:06:56.880 --> 00:07:00.000
It gives you a little more space from which to meet what comes next.
